\newlabel{fig:curriculum}{{3}{5}{Training curriculum. We first stabilized lane movement and anti-idle behavior, then strengthened target semantics and lane aggression, and finally simplified the submitted policy around efficient win conversion after recall proved unreliable}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces External and behavioral performance evidence. The leaderboard result is the main final result: rank 3, 131/67 over 198 games. The lane-pressure plot is more faithful than a total reward curve because it separates own tower HP, enemy tower HP, and kill-death behavior.}}{5}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:performance}{{4}{5}{External and behavioral performance evidence. The leaderboard result is the main final result: rank 3, 131/67 over 198 games. The lane-pressure plot is more faithful than a total reward curve because it separates own tower HP, enemy tower HP, and kill-death behavior}{figure.4}{}}
